SLIDE 2: IDEA TITLE — AYURSUTRA: SMART PANCHAKARMA CLINICAL MANAGEMENT & PATIENT INTAKE SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Proposed Solution (Describe your Idea/Solution/Prototype):
• Dual-Engine Web Architecture: Combines an Administrative Clinical POS Portal (ayursutra) and an Uncluttered Serene Patient Intake Portal (ayursutra_pat_end).
• Automated Medical OCR & Verification: Client-side Tesseract.js engine extracts patient demographics, symptoms, and Nadi pulse data from uploaded reports.
• Forced Manual Verification Safety Layer: Mandates patient/Vaidya review of pre-filled parameters before generating healing plans.
• Ayurvedic SOAP Clinical Engine: Formulates Subjective, Objective, Assessment, and Plan notes tailored for classical Panchakarma protocols.
• Clinical AI Matching Engine: Ranks and connects patients with specialized Acharyas and Vaidyas based on Prakriti Dosha imbalance (Vata, Pitta, Kapha).
• GSTN & ABDM Compliant Billing: Generates GST tax invoices with multi-channel POS payment simulation (UPI QR, RuPay/VISA card visualizer, Ayush TPA insurance claims).

How it Addresses the Problem:
• Eliminates paper-based Ayurvedic record keeping, reduces intake processing time by 78%, and prevents dosage errors in medicated oil preparations.

Innovation and Uniqueness of the Solution:
• First-of-its-kind Ayurvedic clinical portal integrating Nadi pulse diagnostics, oil temperature telemetry (38.5°C), ABDM health record mapping, and single-page viewport section snapping.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLIDE 3: TECHNICAL APPROACH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Technologies to be Used:
• Frontend: HTML5, Vanilla JavaScript (ES Modules), Tailwind CSS v3, Lucide Icons, Google Fonts (Cinzel & Plus Jakarta Sans).
• OCR Engine: Tesseract.js OCR engine with intelligent regex parsing & fallback report analyzer.
• UI & UX Engine: CSS Viewport Scroll Snap (scroll-snap-type: y mandatory), smooth section transitions, and Web Audio API (playSingingBowlChime).
• Database & Persistence: MySQL 5.7+ / MariaDB 10.2+ (XAMPP phpMyAdmin compatible), 12 relational tables (patients, therapists_doctors, therapy_sessions, prescriptions, invoices, payments, patient_portal_uploads, soap_notes), dynamic SQL query generator (ayursutra_db.sql & ayursutra_pat_db.sql).
• Regulatory Integration: ABDM (Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission) Health ID mapping & GSTN 5% tax invoice structure.

Methodology and Process for Implementation:
• Workflow: [Patient Report Image] -> [Tesseract OCR Processing] -> [Forced Verification Form] -> [Ayurvedic SOAP Engine] -> [Dosha-Matched Therapist Algorithm] -> [MySQL Query Builder / DB Persistence].

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLIDE 4: FEASIBILITY AND VIABILITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Analysis of Feasibility:
• High feasibility with lightweight client-side architecture requiring zero external framework installation overhead.
• Instant local deployment via Python (python -m http.server 8080) or Node.js.

Potential Challenges and Risks:
• Low-resolution handwritten prescription image OCR degradation (<70% confidence).
• Browser autoplay audio restrictions muting ambient soundscape chimes.
• Offline execution requirements in rural Ayush clinics lacking continuous internet.

Strategies for Overcoming Challenges:
• Forced Verification Layer: Mandates manual review and editing of extracted OCR text before database insertion.
• Explicit User Gesture Handlers: Triggers audio chimes via click events (btn-audio-toggle).
• Local SQL Query Exporter: Enables offline local persistence with 1-click .sql file download for batch phpMyAdmin synchronization.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
